IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XX.1 -- DOCUMENTS IN ELECTRONIC OR OTHER FORM
-- (ss 252.1 to 252.7). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE READS THE TEXT.
--   * Each section says when a requirement is "satisfied" by an electronic document. A rule here answers
--     whether it is, from the facts the section names.
--   * What the regulations prescribe (the manner of consent, further requirements, a different system) is
--     not among the sources. Each such matter is a plain BOOLEAN input: "the regulations, if any, have been
--     complied with" is TRUE when there are none or they were complied with, and the caller says which.
--   * Section 252.6 gives "electronic document" and "secure electronic signature" the meaning they have in
--     the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act; that Act is not among the sources, so
--     those two are plain inputs there.

§ `Part XX.1 -- Documents in electronic or other form`

§§ `s 252.1 -- definitions`

-- "Any form of representation of information or of concepts fixed in any medium in or by electronic, optical
-- or other similar means and that can be read or perceived by a person or by any means". The three limbs
-- are joined by "and". Section 252.6 has its own meaning, taken in that section.
-- src:3137 | electronic document means, except in section 252.6, any form of representation of information or of concepts fixed in any medium in or by electronic, optical or other similar means and that can be read or perceived by a person or by any means. (document électronique)
@ref CBCA s 252.1 "electronic document" (src:3137)
GIVEN `it is a form of representation of information or of concepts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is fixed in a medium in or by electronic, optical or other similar means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be read or perceived by a person or by any means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `electronic document within s 252.1` IF
        `it is a form of representation of information or of concepts`
    AND `it is fixed in a medium in or by electronic, optical or other similar means`
    AND `it can be read or perceived by a person or by any means`

-- src:3138 | information system means a system used to generate, send, receive, store, or otherwise process an electronic document. (système d’information)
@ref CBCA s 252.1 "information system" (src:3138)
GIVEN `it is a system used to generate, send, receive, store or otherwise process an electronic document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `information system within s 252.1` IF
    `it is a system used to generate, send, receive, store or otherwise process an electronic document`

§§ `s 252.2 -- application`

-- The Part does not apply to two things: a notice, document or other information sent to or issued by the
-- Director pursuant to this Act, and anything prescribed. Either is enough to take it outside the Part.
-- src:3140 | 252.2 This Part does not apply to a notice, document or other information sent to or issued by the Director pursuant to this Act or to any prescribed notice, document or other information.
@ref CBCA s 252.2 (src:3140)
GIVEN `the notice, document or other information is sent to or issued by the Director pursuant to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice, document or other information is prescribed to be outside the Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part XX.1 applies within s 252.2` IF
        (NOT `the notice, document or other information is sent to or issued by the Director pursuant to this Act`)
    AND (NOT `the notice, document or other information is prescribed to be outside the Part`)

§§ `s 252.3 -- use not mandatory; consent`

-- src:3142 | 252.3 (1) Nothing in this Act or the regulations requires a person to create or provide an electronic document.
@ref CBCA s 252.3(1) (src:3142)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act or the regulations require a person to create or provide an electronic document within s 252.3(1)` MEANS FALSE

-- (2): "despite anything in this Part", a requirement to provide a person with a notice, document or other
-- information is not satisfied by an electronic document unless (a) the addressee has consented in the
-- prescribed manner AND designated an information system, and (b) the document is provided to the designated
-- system, unless otherwise prescribed. (3): the addressee may revoke the consent in the prescribed manner;
-- the text does not say what revocation does, so a revoked consent is read as no longer a consent
-- (fork F-252.3-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3144 | (2) Despite anything in this Part, a requirement under this Act or the regulations to provide a person with a notice, document or other information is not satisfied by the provision of an electronic document unless
-- src:3145 | (a) the addressee has consented, in the manner prescribed, and has designated an information system for the receipt of the electronic document; and
-- src:3146 | (b) the electronic document is provided to the designated information system, unless otherwise prescribed.
@ref CBCA s 252.3(2) (src:3144-3146)
GIVEN `the addressee has consented in the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the addressee has revoked the consent in the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the addressee has designated an information system for the receipt of the electronic document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic document is provided to the designated information system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations otherwise prescribe how the electronic document is to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision of an electronic document satisfies the requirement to provide it to the addressee within s 252.3(2)` IF
        `the addressee has consented in the manner prescribed`
    AND (NOT `the addressee has revoked the consent in the manner prescribed`)
    AND `the addressee has designated an information system for the receipt of the electronic document`
    AND (    `the electronic document is provided to the designated information system`
         OR  `the regulations otherwise prescribe how the electronic document is to be provided`)

-- src:3148 | (3) An addressee may revoke the consent referred to in paragraph (2)(a) in the manner prescribed.
@ref CBCA s 252.3(3) (src:3148)
GIVEN `the addressee has consented under paragraph 252.3(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the addressee revokes the consent in the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the revocation takes effect within s 252.3(3)` IF
        `the addressee has consented under paragraph 252.3(2)(a)`
    AND `the addressee revokes the consent in the manner prescribed`

§§ `s 252.4 -- creation and provision of information`

-- "If (a) the by-laws or the articles do not provide otherwise; and (b) the regulations, if any, have been
-- complied with."
-- src:3150 | 252.4 A requirement under this Act or the regulations that a notice, document or other information be created or provided, is satisfied by the creation or provision of an electronic document if
-- src:3151 | (a) the by-laws or the articles of the corporation do not provide otherwise; and
-- src:3152 | (b) the regulations, if any, have been complied with.
@ref CBCA s 252.4 (src:3150-3152)
GIVEN `the by-laws or the articles of the corporation provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations, if any, have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an electronic document satisfies the requirement to create or provide within s 252.4` IF
        (NOT `the by-laws or the articles of the corporation provide otherwise`)
    AND `the regulations, if any, have been complied with`

-- Where the requirement is to provide a notice, document or other information to a person, section 252.3(2)
-- applies "despite anything in this Part", so both rules must be met. This is a composition of two rules of
-- the text, not a sentence of it.
-- src:3144 | (2) Despite anything in this Part, a requirement under this Act or the regulations to provide a person with a notice, document or other information is not satisfied by the provision of an electronic document unless
@ref CBCA s 252.3(2), s 252.4 composition (src:3144)
GIVEN `the electronic document satisfies the requirement to create or provide under section 252.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision satisfies the requirement to provide it to the addressee under subsection 252.3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an electronic document satisfies a requirement to provide a notice to a person within s 252.3(2) and s 252.4` IF
        `the electronic document satisfies the requirement to create or provide under section 252.4`
    AND `the provision satisfies the requirement to provide it to the addressee under subsection 252.3(2)`

§§ `s 252.5 -- in writing; copies; registered mail`

-- (1): "in addition to the conditions in section 252.4".
-- src:3154 | 252.5 (1) A requirement under this Act or the regulations that a notice, document or other information be created in writing is satisfied by the creation of an electronic document if, in addition to the conditions in section 252.4,
-- src:3155 | (a) the information in the electronic document is accessible so as to be usable for subsequent reference; and
-- src:3156 | (b) the regulations pertaining to this subsection, if any, have been complied with.
@ref CBCA s 252.5(1) (src:3154-3156)
GIVEN `the conditions in section 252.4 are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information in the electronic document is accessible so as to be usable for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations pertaining to subsection 252.5(1), if any, have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an electronic document satisfies the requirement to create in writing within s 252.5(1)` IF
        `the conditions in section 252.4 are met`
    AND `the information in the electronic document is accessible so as to be usable for subsequent reference`
    AND `the regulations pertaining to subsection 252.5(1), if any, have been complied with`

-- src:3158 | (2) A requirement under this Act or the regulations that a notice, document or other information be provided in writing is satisfied by the provision of an electronic document if, in addition to the conditions set out in section 252.4,
-- src:3159 | (a) the information in the electronic document is accessible by the addressee and capable of being retained by the addressee, so as to be usable for subsequent reference; and
-- src:3160 | (b) the regulations pertaining to this subsection, if any, have been complied with.
@ref CBCA s 252.5(2) (src:3158-3160)
GIVEN `the conditions set out in section 252.4 are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information in the electronic document is accessible by the addressee and capable of being retained by the addressee, so as to be usable for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations pertaining to subsection 252.5(2), if any, have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an electronic document satisfies the requirement to provide in writing within s 252.5(2)` IF
        `the conditions set out in section 252.4 are met`
    AND `the information in the electronic document is accessible by the addressee and capable of being retained by the addressee, so as to be usable for subsequent reference`
    AND `the regulations pertaining to subsection 252.5(2), if any, have been complied with`

-- (3): the requirement is for one or more copies to a single addressee at the same time; a single version
-- of the electronic document satisfies it.
-- src:3162 | (3) A requirement under this Act or the regulations for one or more copies of a document to be provided to a single addressee at the same time is satisfied by the provision of a single version of the electronic document.
@ref CBCA s 252.5(3) (src:3162)
GIVEN `the requirement is for one or more copies of a document to be provided to a single addressee at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a single version of the electronic document is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a single version of an electronic document satisfies the requirement for copies within s 252.5(3)` IF
        `the requirement is for one or more copies of a document to be provided to a single addressee at the same time`
    AND `a single version of the electronic document is provided`

-- (4): sending an electronic document does not satisfy a requirement to provide a document by registered
-- mail, unless prescribed.
-- src:3164 | (4) A requirement under this Act or the regulations to provide a document by registered mail is not satisfied by the sending of an electronic document unless prescribed.
@ref CBCA s 252.5(4) (src:3164)
GIVEN `the requirement is to provide a document by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations prescribe that sending an electronic document satisfies it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sending an electronic document satisfies the requirement to provide by registered mail within s 252.5(4)` IF
        `the requirement is to provide a document by registered mail`
    AND `the regulations prescribe that sending an electronic document satisfies it`

§§ `s 252.6 -- statutory declarations and affidavits`

-- Section 252.6(1): both signatures with a secure electronic signature, and ss 252.3 to 252.5 complied
-- with; "electronic document" and "secure electronic signature" take the meaning given in the Personal
-- Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (an Act that is not among the sources), so those are
-- plain inputs.
-- src:3166 | 252.6 (1) A statutory declaration or an affidavit required under this Act or the regulations may be created or provided in an electronic document if
-- src:3167 | (a) the person who makes the statutory declaration or affidavit signs it with his or her secure electronic signature;
-- src:3168 | (b) the authorized person before whom the statutory declaration or affidavit is made signs it with his or her secure electronic signature; and
-- src:3169 | (c) the requirements of sections 252.3 to 252.5 are complied with.
@ref CBCA s 252.6(1) (src:3166-3169)
GIVEN `the person who makes the statutory declaration or affidavit signs it with his or her secure electronic signature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorized person before whom the statutory declaration or affidavit is made signs it with his or her secure electronic signature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of sections 252.3 to 252.5 are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a statutory declaration or affidavit may be created or provided in an electronic document within s 252.6(1)` IF
        `the person who makes the statutory declaration or affidavit signs it with his or her secure electronic signature`
    AND `the authorized person before whom the statutory declaration or affidavit is made signs it with his or her secure electronic signature`
    AND `the requirements of sections 252.3 to 252.5 are complied with`

-- (2) and (3): the two defined terms take the meaning in subsection 31(1) of the Personal Information
-- Protection and Electronic Documents Act, and in paragraph (1)(c) the references in ss 252.3 to 252.5 are to
-- that meaning. The Act is not among the sources.
-- src:3171 | (2) For the purposes of this section, electronic document and secure electronic signature have the same meaning as in subsection 31(1) of the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act.
-- src:3173 | (3) For the purpose of complying with paragraph (1)(c), the references to an electronic document in sections 252.3 to 252.5 are to be read as references to an “electronic document” as defined in subsection 31(1) of the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act.
@ref CBCA s 252.6(2), s 252.6(3) (src:3171 src:3173)
GIVEN `it is an electronic document within the meaning of subsection 31(1) of the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: that Act is not among the sources
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `electronic document within s 252.6` IF
    `it is an electronic document within the meaning of subsection 31(1) of the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act`

§§ `s 252.7 -- signatures`

-- "Except with respect to a statutory declaration or an affidavit"; the prescribed requirements, if any, are
-- met; and the signature results from a technology or process that permits all three of (a), (b), (c) to be
-- proven.
-- src:3175 | 252.7 A requirement under this Act or the regulations for a signature or for a document to be executed, except with respect to a statutory declaration or an affidavit, is satisfied if, in relation to an electronic document, the prescribed requirements pertaining to this section, if any, are met and if the signature results from the application by a person of a technology or a process that permits the following to be proven:
-- src:3176 | (a) the signature resulting from the use by a person of the technology or process is unique to the person;
-- src:3177 | (b) the technology or process is used by a person to incorporate, attach or associate the person’s signature to the electronic document; and
-- src:3178 | (c) the technology or process can be used to identify the person using the technology or process.
@ref CBCA s 252.7 (src:3175-3178)
GIVEN `the document is a statutory declaration or an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed requirements pertaining to section 252.7, if any, are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be proven that the signature resulting from the use by a person of the technology or process is unique to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be proven that the technology or process is used by a person to incorporate, attach or associate the person's signature to the electronic document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be proven that the technology or process can be used to identify the person using it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a requirement for a signature or for a document to be executed is satisfied within s 252.7` IF
        (NOT `the document is a statutory declaration or an affidavit`)
    AND `the prescribed requirements pertaining to section 252.7, if any, are met`
    AND `it can be proven that the signature resulting from the use by a person of the technology or process is unique to the person`
    AND `it can be proven that the technology or process is used by a person to incorporate, attach or associate the person's signature to the electronic document`
    AND `it can be proven that the technology or process can be used to identify the person using it`
